From dfc1bba10fe27fed849ede69bbfc8eba1500cc05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 17:55:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] smart connect: drop the model-specific 6 GHz sentence from
 the "- -" note

The note explained that a "- -" column means the band is not in the Smart Connect
group, then asserted that 6 GHz is left out by default "on this model". That is
only true where the defaults ship it that way, and the page is shown on every
model. It was also redundant - whichever radios are in the group is already
visible in the columns above it. The rest of the note is model-agnostic and stays.
---
 release/src/router/www/Advanced_Smart_Connect.asp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/Advanced_Smart_Connect.asp b/release/src/router/www/Advanced_Smart_Connect.asp
index d4fe47ac931..5f1d60611ee 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/Advanced_Smart_Connect.asp
+++ b/release/src/router/www/Advanced_Smart_Connect.asp
@@ -1083,7 +1083,7 @@ function toggleSmartConnect(){
 			     re-shown the moment the band is added back. Shown only when a column is
 			     actually suppressed - see genSmartConnectExcludedNote(). -->
 			<div id="sc_excluded_note" class="formfontdesc" style="display:none;line-height:18px;margin:10px 5px;padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid #6b8fa3;border-radius:4px;background:rgba(107,143,163,0.10);">
-				<b>Some bands show &ldquo;- -&rdquo;.</b> Those radios are not part of the Smart Connect group, so there are no steering rules to display for them. Nothing has been lost &mdash; each band keeps its own policy and it reappears here as soon as the band is added back. Choose which radios take part under <b>Wireless &gt; General</b>. Note that 6 GHz is left out of Smart Connect by default on this model.
+				<b>Some bands show &ldquo;- -&rdquo;.</b> Those radios are not part of the Smart Connect group, so there are no steering rules to display for them. Nothing has been lost &mdash; each band keeps its own policy and it reappears here as soon as the band is added back. Choose which radios take part under <b>Wireless &gt; General</b>.
 			</div>
 			<div id="bsd_steering_div">
 				<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" bordercolor="#6b8fa3" border="1" align="center" width="100%" class="FormTable" style="margin-top:10px">
-- 
2.25.1

